+# Advisor Email Draft, 2026-06-19
+
+Subject: Current-five evidence decisions before next capture or expansion
+
+Dear Professor Singh,
+
+I have consolidated the current five Week 2 evidence bundles into one evidence
+packet and one fillable decision sheet:
+
+- Evidence packet: `docs/research/current_five_evidence_packet_2026-06-19.md`
+- Decision sheet: `data/current_five_decision_sheet_2026-06-19.csv`
+
+The current evidence package is unchanged: Week 2 sanity is `ready`, the cycle
+is `completed`, and the research package has 42 audit reports and 20
+longitudinal summaries. The 8 CMP/manual-review rows are still pending.
+
+The five current sites now separate into:
+
+| Site | Current evidence treatment |
+|---|---|
+| The Guardian | Banner-present evidence card; visible controls in screenshot. |
+| Coca-Cola | Banner-present evidence card; visible Privacy Preference Center in screenshot. |
+| CNN | No-visible-banner contrast candidate. |
+| Booking.com | No-visible-banner contrast candidate. |
+| NerdWallet | No-visible-banner contrast candidate. |
+
+Before I run another capture or expand the sample, I need three decisions:
+
+1. For The Guardian and Coca-Cola, should I confirm them as banner-present
+   evidence cards, manually override then score them, wait for a rerun, or
+   replace them before expansion?
+2. For CNN, Booking.com, and NerdWallet, should they stay as a separate
+   no-visible-banner contrast group, move into the main RQ1 table with a clear
+   label, wait for rerun evidence, or be replaced before expansion?
+3. For the next work block, should I rerun the current five with the fixed
+   capture agent, manually validate the current evidence cards before
+   expanding, expand banner-present candidates first, or resolve the 8 pending
+   CMP/manual-review rows first?
+
+My proposed next step is: manually validate the current five first, keep
+CNN/Booking.com/NerdWallet as a labeled no-visible-banner contrast group for
+now, and then expand toward the roughly 20-site deep sample with priority on
+sites that show visible banner/control evidence.
+
+Best,
+Qianyi
